<main class="center">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class='underline'>About Us</h1>
    
    <section>
      <h2 class="fs-0">Achaea</h2>
      <p>
        Hi everyone! My name is <strong class="h2-color">Achaea</strong>. I work as a registered nurse and I love working with different crafts as a side hobby. 
        I love cooking, shelling and video games. I enjoy turning things I've collected, shells on the beach or upcycling old jewelry, into my own little creations.
      </p>
      <p>
        Different crafts I work with are beading, 3d printing, needle felting, embroidery, crochet, jewelry making and resin creations. Feel Free to email me if
        you ever want anything custom made.
      </p>
    </section>
    
    <section>
      <h2 class="fs-0">Kevin</h2>
      <p>
        My name is <strong class="h2-color">Kevin</strong> and I'm a bit of a nerd who's into board games, video games and working out. I've used PCs since I was 
        roughly 8 <em>(for gaming)</em> but I never considered a career involved with computers until recently. I've had this idea that just because I like food doesn't 
        mean I would enjoy, or even be, a good chef <strong>(it would be a nightmare career personally)</strong>. Thankfully though, that analogy didn't apply to 
        my enjoyment, or ability, to learn how to cookup websites!
      </p>
      <p>
        I started learning web development through <%= link_to 'The Odin Project', "https://www.theodinproject.com/"%> mid-2022 in my offtime and something just 
        clicked. It wasn't easy to keep myself accountable and set my own pace, but it's just so satisfying to create something with just words and numbers.
      </p>
      <p>
        This was my first project that wasn't an assignemnt, and it made me fall in love with Rails, aka <a href="https://rubyonrails.org/">Ruby on Rails</a>.
        After gaining more experience, using other frameworks like Express.js and Vue.js for <a href="https://github.com/Soadaa56?tab=repositories">other projects</a>, 
        dabbling a bit with squarespace for a client, I've grown to apperciate Rails even more.  It has its pros and cons, like anything else, but it is a pleasure 
        to use for sure.
      </p>
    </section>

